WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.

2
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.340
We were on The Office together.

4
00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:08.580
And we're best friends.

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.

6
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

7
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:20.560
We're The Office ladies.

8
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.460
Hi, Jenna.

9
00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:26.920
Are you in the inner circle?

10
00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.220
I'm probably not.

11
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:32.920
I think I've spent my whole life outside of the inner circle.

12
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.780
Same, which is why we became best friends.

13
00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:44.060
This is Season 7, Episode 23, written by Charlie Grandy and directed by Matt Soane.

14
00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:51.520
Angela, when I read you this summary, I think it's going to become very clear to you that Ainsley wrote it, starting with the very first word.

15
00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.360
Enigmatic new boss D'Angelo.

16
00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:55.980
Did you see?

17
00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:57.840
I would not write enigmatic.

18
00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.860
That's a five-star vocab word.

19
00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:06.700
Enigmatic new boss D'Angelo seems to have an inner circle of favorite male employees.

20
00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:08.680
Which has caused a divide in the office.

21
00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:12.600
Later, D'Angelo's competitive side lands him in the hospital.

22
00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:14.000
Pretty straightforward.

23
00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:14.660
Mm-hmm.

24
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.260
Let's jump into Fast Fact number one.

25
00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.380
This episode aired on May 5th, 2011.

26
00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:23.320
It was originally titled Sexism.

27
00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:24.220
Oh.

28
00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:29.660
But Greg gave the note that he thought that the sexism storyline was kind of a nice plot twiSt.

29
00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:34.020
And if we named it sexism, then the title would give that twist away.

30
00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:35.640
So they changed it to inner circle.

31
00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:40.980
Randy shared with us that this episode originally came in one minute too long.

32
00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:42.300
One minute.

33
00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:43.600
And they had to trim it?

34
00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:48.720
Well, first, Greg and Paul pushed the studio to let them have an extra minute of airtime.

35
00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:52.800
But that would mean that the studio would have to sell one minute less ads.

36
00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:54.680
So guess what they said?

37
00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:55.720
They said, nope.

38
00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:57.360
That was a hard pass.

39
00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:00.580
They suggested that we cut the credits down.

40
00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:02.180
Because we've done that before.

41
00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:02.560
Yeah.

42
00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:06.640
But Greg and Paul felt that it was really important to establish the new credit sequence

43
00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.180
with Steve leaving.

44
00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:12.500
So eventually, they found a way to edit the episode down to the standard

45
00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:15.780
21 minutes and 35 seconds of running time.

46
00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:20.160
Well, if you guys have the DVDs, there's some real nuggets and deleted scenes.

47
00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:21.800
And now that makes sense to me.

48
00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:23.720
And I'm going to share some of them in this episode.

49
00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:24.760
Very good.

50
00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:28.280
Fast fact number two, this episode was a bottle show.

51
00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:29.800
We've talked about those before.

52
00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:34.940
And because it was so contained, we were actually able to shoot this episode in only four days

53
00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:36.800
rather than the usual five days.

54
00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:38.740
I bet everyone was excited about that.

55
00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:40.420
Well, we did not get a day off.

56
00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:40.880
Oh.

57
00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:46.320
We used the extra day to do that extra shooting on Goodbye, Michael.

58
00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:47.480
Oh.

59
00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:51.780
Now, you know, these bottle shows, the idea of them is that they're supposed to be very

60
00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:54.060
easy, very drama-free episodes.

61
00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:54.640
Yeah.

62
00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:58.580
No big, like, stunts, no big to-dos, no craziness.

63
00:02:58.940 --> 00:02:59.840
No locations.

64
00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:00.660
Nothing.

65
00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:05.760
Well, this was not a drama-free episode.

66
00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:08.300
First, we had the running time drama.

67
00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:08.840
Right.

68
00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:10.340
That was a bunch of emails back and forth.

69
00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:14.240
Then Randy said there was a standards and practices drama.

70
00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:15.540
For what?

71
00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:17.140
You're going to have to wait for it.

72
00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:18.000
Oh.

73
00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:19.560
I'm racking my brain.

74
00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:21.860
What did they get all out of Tizzy about?

75
00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:22.500
I know.

76
00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.660
There was an ad sales drama.

77
00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:26.220
There was a music drama.

78
00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:28.060
And we'll get to it.

79
00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:29.300
There was a stunt.

80
00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:30.280
Oh, yeah.

81
00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:31.000
Terribly wrong.

82
00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:31.540
Yeah.

83
00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:34.280
That's the one I thought you were going to lead with because...

84
00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:37.580
You guys, we almost, like, seriously injured Will Ferrell.

85
00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:38.640
Yeah.

86
00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.220
We'll get to it.

87
00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:40.740
Yeah.

88
00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:41.480
Yeah.

89
00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:42.500
It was crazy.

90
00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:44.380
Fast fact number three.

91
00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:47.320
This was our first episode without Steve.

92
00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:50.160
It was our last episode with Will Ferrell.

93
00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:56.540
We got a fan question from Katie B in Dallas, Texas, who wanted to know, how was it the first

94
00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.020
day on set without Steve?

95
00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:00.940
Katie, it was bizarre.

96
00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:03.120
It was super weird.

97
00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:03.620
Yeah.

98
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:11.140
When I watched the credit sequence in this episode and he wasn't in it, I was crushed.

99
00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:16.560
Like, and it kind of reminds me, like, that's what it was like to show up.

100
00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:18.520
And then he wasn't in hair and makeup.

101
00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:23.080
He wasn't there to talk to us about his favorite pizza.

102
00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.560
It was super odd.

103
00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:27.280
And we loved Will.

104
00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:30.620
Like, thank goodness for Will and the positive energy he brought.

105
00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:37.580
But it was just flat out weird going to work without the main person we had all sort of

106
00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:41.060
been working around as a cast, his character.

107
00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:44.000
It was, it was really, it was really crazy, Katie.

108
00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:46.180
Well, listen, that's all I got.

109
00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:48.200
Fast facts were literally fast today.

110
00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:51.380
I have a new DVD alert.

111
00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:52.540
Oh.

112
00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:54.240
Like, why do I say alert?

113
00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:55.320
Alert.

114
00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:56.700
Breaking news.

115
00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:05.320
Seven, for those of you who are rewatching with the DVD box set, here are a few of the

116
00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:06.500
features on this DVD.

117
00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:13.300
In addition to the usual deleted scenes, there is a commentary, and there is also a great

118
00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:17.020
blooper reel and the webisode series, The Third Floor.

119
00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:23.260
Angela, when Randy sent us all his facts for this episode this week, he said he was very

120
00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:29.840
sad to put that last DVD in his player because, you know, he leaves us at the end of the

121
00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:30.300
season.

122
00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:30.740
Yeah.

123
00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:35.900
So we had Steve exit during the season and Randy exited at the end of the season.

124
00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:39.300
It was an emotional last few episodes.

125
00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:40.740
Yeah, it was.

126
00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:41.840
All right.

127
00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:44.260
Well, should we take a break and then get right to it?

128
00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:45.180
Let's do it.

129
00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:56.820
This episode opens with a conference room meeting.

130
00:05:57.480 --> 00:05:59.380
D'Angelo is laying down the law.

131
00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:03.200
And anyone who doesn't like how he does things can just walk right out the door.

132
00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:05.320
But they're all things people like.

133
00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:07.140
Like, he wants to end the workday at five.

134
00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:09.820
He wants to have ice cream on Thursdays.

135
00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:12.920
He tells Daryl, I'm going to give you a full ride.

136
00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:15.780
We're going to pay for you to go to business school.

137
00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:17.480
Deal with it.

138
00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:22.540
At 23 seconds, I don't know if you noticed, but Daryl is back to wearing his shirt and tie.

139
00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:23.940
I did notice.

140
00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:26.960
I also caught what I think might be an improv.

141
00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:32.420
When Daryl says, seriously, D'Angelo says, stone cold, seriously.

142
00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:34.360
I looked in the script.

143
00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:36.080
That line was not there.

144
00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:40.080
In the script, D'Angelo just says, no, I'm kidding.

145
00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:40.980
Yes, I'm serious.

146
00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:44.060
So I wonder if this is a little bit of Will Ferrell.

147
00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:48.280
I absolutely loved Craig Robinson's performance in this whole episode.

148
00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:52.820
If you watch this episode, you have to watch all of his reactions in the background.

149
00:06:53.820 --> 00:06:55.160
Every line he delivers.

150
00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:55.880
I don't know.

151
00:06:55.980 --> 00:06:58.700
This was like an I love Craig Robinson episode for me.

152
00:06:59.060 --> 00:06:59.960
He is great.

153
00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:02.680
And I love the Daryl storyline of him going to night school.

154
00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:05.380
I do have a little bit of a bust on Craig.

155
00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:06.380
What's that?

156
00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:09.460
At one minute, you can totally see him starting to break.

157
00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:14.280
His shoulders are shaking because I think this part wasn't scripted as well.

158
00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:19.120
When D'Angelo is saying, and Toby, you're getting a new chair, whether he likes it or not.

159
00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:20.720
Toby says, thanks.

160
00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.260
And D'Angelo says, don't thank me.

161
00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:25.140
Hey, don't thank me, guy.

162
00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:27.000
That wasn't in the script.

163
00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:30.260
And you can see Craig's like shoulders like shaking.

164
00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:36.020
I mean, we should say that Will like would improvise here and there and we would all lose it.

165
00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:38.140
Will can read the phone book and be funny.

166
00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:40.800
I mean, every line he says is funny.

167
00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:42.280
All right.

168
00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:45.040
So now the episode begins.

169
00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:55.180
D'Angelo and Daryl are arriving to work and Pam is going to interrupt their chat to tell him about her friend Carla, who might make a great executive assistant.

170
00:07:55.600 --> 00:08:04.840
I remember that the NBC photographer was here this day when we were shooting this and they took pictures of this scene and I charged them.

171
00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:05.880
I bet.

172
00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:09.860
Well, you know, Pam's runner with the resumes was bigger.

173
00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:11.620
There's more of it in deleted scenes.

174
00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:12.800
I'm going to share some of it.

175
00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:20.980
But one of the things that tickled me, Jenna, is I'm such a nerd for this, for whatever character gets to say the title of a movie or an episode.

176
00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:22.420
I just think it's so cool.

177
00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:25.200
And Pam gets to say the title of this episode.

178
00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:25.740
Really?

179
00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:26.260
Yeah.

180
00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:30.880
She says to Jim, oh, is that what he says in your little inner circle meetings?

181
00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:32.020
Oh, yes, you're right.

182
00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:33.600
I was like, ah, she said the title.

183
00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:34.880
I'm a dork for stuff like that.

184
00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:36.440
You point it out every time.

185
00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:36.780
I know.

186
00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:37.300
It's very cute.

187
00:08:37.420 --> 00:08:37.660
Okay.

188
00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:40.640
We got a fan catch from Aiden W.

189
00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:44.900
in Portland, Oregon, who said, there are three Carlas in the office.

190
00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:53.280
There is Carla, the mission trip leader, Carla, Pam's executive assistant friend, and coming up, Carla Fern, Andy's agent.

191
00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:56.300
What are the writers' obsession with the name Carla?

192
00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:58.940
I've personally never met a Carla in my life.

193
00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:00.220
Wow.

194
00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:01.820
I didn't realize there were three.

195
00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:03.440
Yeah, three Carlas.

196
00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:04.780
That's such a great catch.

197
00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:08.040
Andy and Pam are convinced there's an inner circle.

198
00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:09.640
Jim's like, no, there's no inner circle.

199
00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:13.060
And Kevin's like, he only says that because he's in it.

200
00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:14.360
And then Kevin is so proud.

201
00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:16.940
He's like, mom, I'm in the inner circle.

202
00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:18.920
I loved that Kevin was in the inner circle.

203
00:09:19.060 --> 00:09:20.140
It was such a nice twiSt.

204
00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:21.560
Unexpected.

205
00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:26.200
Someone who is not in the inner circle or who doesn't want to be in the inner circle.

206
00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:30.180
And D'Angelo is doing everything he can to get Dwight on his good side.

207
00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:32.360
He tries to bring him a coffee from downstairs.

208
00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:33.920
Dwight throws it in the trash.

209
00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:34.920
Not interested.

210
00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:35.920
Not interested.

211
00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:44.620
As soon as D'Angelo tries to entice Dwight with like some beers, and he said they can listen to Automatic for the People on his jukebox.

212
00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:53.280
Lady, I could not stop laughing because I have a little bit of backstory about the album Automatic for the People.

213
00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:54.480
What?

214
00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:55.280
Okay.

215
00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:57.080
I don't know this album.

216
00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:58.040
Who sings this album?

217
00:09:58.360 --> 00:09:58.420
Oh, my God.

218
00:09:58.420 --> 00:09:59.200
It's R.E.M.

219
00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:00.220
You do know this album.

220
00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:00.640
You do.

221
00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:01.420
I promise you.

222
00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:01.680
Okay.

223
00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:02.000
Okay.

224
00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:06.600
So it came out while I was in college in October 1992.

225
00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:08.740
You guys, I know I'm a dinosaur.

226
00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:12.820
But when it came out, I was going through a breakup.

227
00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:19.680
And I'm sorry I laughed, but I just like I know these moments where like, oh, this was your breakup album.

228
00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:20.100
Yes.

229
00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:22.100
Did you listen to it just so much?

230
00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:25.660
Oh, there was one song that instantly takes me back to that time.

231
00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:26.860
It starts with this piano.

232
00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:28.100
The song is called Night Swimming.

233
00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:29.500
I need you to hear a little bit of it.

234
00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:34.780
And then I am going to read you an entry from my journal during this breakup.

235
00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:37.140
You have made my day.

236
00:10:58.460 --> 00:10:58.880
Okay.

237
00:10:58.880 --> 00:10:59.240
Okay.

238
00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:00.320
You're getting the idea right.

239
00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:01.120
I'm in a mood.

240
00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:02.140
You're in a mood.

241
00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:02.900
I'm feeling it.

242
00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:04.540
Now I'm almost curled up in a ball.

243
00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:05.020
Okay.

244
00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:07.120
Now I'm opening my journal.

245
00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:07.740
Okay.

246
00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:08.160
Here we go.

247
00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:09.220
It's super old.

248
00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:15.600
First of all, you guys should know, I hadn't been dating this guy very long, so I wasn't like super heartbroken.

249
00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:17.280
I was more just really ticked off.

250
00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:17.860
Okay.

251
00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:18.260
Okay.

252
00:11:18.460 --> 00:11:18.700
Okay.

253
00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:21.480
So, picture me listening to Night Swimming.

254
00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:22.480
I'm ticked off.

255
00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:23.580
Here we go.

256
00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:26.200
October 17th, 1992.

257
00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:28.040
Okay.

