1187
00:48:51.640 --> 00:48:55.940
How did you guys do the scene when D'Angelo does the basketball dunk?

1188
00:48:56.760 --> 00:48:59.920
Well, everyone, this was our stunt gone horribly wrong.

1189
00:49:00.480 --> 00:49:04.680
When Greg was in the studio with us, we asked him if he remembered this moment.

1190
00:49:05.120 --> 00:49:06.020
He did.

1191
00:49:06.640 --> 00:49:07.960
Here's what he had to say.

1192
00:49:08.540 --> 00:49:10.780
I still think about that constantly.

1193
00:49:11.000 --> 00:49:12.000
It was horrible.

1194
00:49:12.200 --> 00:49:14.180
And, you know, I wasn't running the show then.

1195
00:49:14.320 --> 00:49:14.760
Paul was.

1196
00:49:14.840 --> 00:49:18.420
And I was coming in to watch and there is Will Ferrell.

1197
00:49:18.420 --> 00:49:25.860
And the joke was that he was going to dunk this basketball in the warehouse and our special

1198
00:49:25.860 --> 00:49:30.900
effects guys had rigged a harness for him and a rope and a pulley.

1199
00:49:31.080 --> 00:49:34.360
And their idea was he's going to run.

1200
00:49:34.500 --> 00:49:36.960
He's going to jump as high as he can jump.

1201
00:49:37.060 --> 00:49:43.100
And then at the very apex of his jump, they were going to yank on this clothesline and he

1202
00:49:43.100 --> 00:49:50.360
was going to seamlessly continue his arc until he was tall enough to dunk and that it would look

1203
00:49:50.360 --> 00:49:51.640
like he could dunk the ball.

1204
00:49:51.880 --> 00:49:57.500
And I had enormous reservations about this, you know, just from the physics of it.

1205
00:49:57.760 --> 00:49:59.620
I was like, I can't understand.

1206
00:49:59.960 --> 00:50:00.120
Skeptical.

1207
00:50:00.260 --> 00:50:00.480
Yeah.

1208
00:50:00.640 --> 00:50:06.180
You know, the idea that his mass is going to just as it just before it starts to go down,

1209
00:50:06.980 --> 00:50:12.100
they're going to like seamlessly keep it going and you're not going to be able to tell.

1210
00:50:12.740 --> 00:50:19.040
So, I was very skeptical, you know, and like the first take, he jumps and then he, you know,

1211
00:50:19.700 --> 00:50:24.280
starts to fall and they start pulling on this thing, you know, and it just looks like this

1212
00:50:24.280 --> 00:50:26.540
weird up and down thing that is not possible.

1213
00:50:26.760 --> 00:50:28.840
And then they're like, no, no, you got to pull harder.

1214
00:50:28.960 --> 00:50:29.960
You didn't pull hard enough.

1215
00:50:29.960 --> 00:50:35.240
And so, the second, you know, the next take, he runs, they yank on this thing and he's

1216
00:50:35.240 --> 00:50:39.540
just pile driven into the rim of the basketball with a sorrowful crash.

1217
00:50:39.900 --> 00:50:44.560
And we're like, oh my God, you know, he was so nice to come help us out, do a few episodes.

1218
00:50:44.560 --> 00:50:47.080
And it was just, it was such a disaster.

1219
00:50:48.160 --> 00:50:49.420
I remember it.

1220
00:50:49.520 --> 00:50:51.060
I will never forget it.

1221
00:50:51.160 --> 00:50:52.200
It was so shocking.

1222
00:50:52.700 --> 00:50:54.200
It was crazy, Angela.

1223
00:50:54.960 --> 00:50:57.620
Like my brain couldn't wrap itself around it.

1224
00:50:57.620 --> 00:51:01.940
Like, I didn't understand how he got from the ground up there so faSt.

1225
00:51:02.260 --> 00:51:04.180
And I remember just being stunned.

1226
00:51:05.080 --> 00:51:10.680
Well, Randy said that the stunt assistants pulled so hard that he flew up much higher than they

1227
00:51:10.680 --> 00:51:11.160
planned.

1228
00:51:11.800 --> 00:51:17.520
His knee got rammed into the basketball hoop and he got a really bad cut on his leg, like

1229
00:51:17.520 --> 00:51:18.480
just below his knee.

1230
00:51:18.800 --> 00:51:21.940
We had to bring our set medic out and all that stuff.

1231
00:51:22.260 --> 00:51:25.840
Randy said he was going to call a rap on it and just be like, forget it.

1232
00:51:25.960 --> 00:51:26.900
We're not doing this again.

1233
00:51:26.900 --> 00:51:32.620
And he said, Will pulled him aside and he said, hey, listen, I don't want you to blame

1234
00:51:32.620 --> 00:51:32.960
anyone.

1235
00:51:32.960 --> 00:51:34.440
I don't want you to punish anyone.

1236
00:51:34.440 --> 00:51:35.340
I am fine.

1237
00:51:35.520 --> 00:51:36.500
I am not in pain.

1238
00:51:36.940 --> 00:51:38.340
I'd like to try it again.

1239
00:51:38.840 --> 00:51:40.240
I mean, what?

1240
00:51:40.980 --> 00:51:41.460
Yeah.

1241
00:51:41.920 --> 00:51:42.620
Will Ferrell.

1242
00:51:42.820 --> 00:51:43.240
I know.

1243
00:51:43.440 --> 00:51:45.700
I would be like, I am going home.

1244
00:51:45.980 --> 00:51:48.320
But I think that like all the time.

1245
00:51:48.320 --> 00:51:52.540
I watch people like tough it out in situations and I'm like, I'm out.

1246
00:51:53.080 --> 00:51:53.560
Goodbye.

1247
00:51:54.220 --> 00:51:57.060
Randy said he allowed one more take at Will's requeSt.

1248
00:51:57.620 --> 00:51:58.920
And at that time.

1249
00:51:59.220 --> 00:52:00.260
They auto corrected.

1250
00:52:00.680 --> 00:52:00.900
Yeah.

1251
00:52:01.080 --> 00:52:05.240
They kind of lifted him and it never really ended up being what they needed.

1252
00:52:05.240 --> 00:52:08.000
But at that point, they were like, we're calling it.

1253
00:52:08.120 --> 00:52:10.300
We're just going to have to go with the footage that we have.

1254
00:52:11.040 --> 00:52:15.700
Randy said that at rap, he walked Will Ferrell to his car and he was just like apologizing

1255
00:52:15.700 --> 00:52:18.100
profusely and saying, like, do you want to go to the ER?

1256
00:52:18.180 --> 00:52:19.700
Like, what can we do for this?

1257
00:52:19.880 --> 00:52:20.660
Cut on your leg.

1258
00:52:21.220 --> 00:52:26.300
And he said that Will looked at him and quoted a famous line from Monty Python and just said,

1259
00:52:26.480 --> 00:52:28.560
tis but a scratch, merely a flesh wound.

1260
00:52:29.360 --> 00:52:31.720
And he assured him, he said, I'll be fine.

1261
00:52:31.860 --> 00:52:33.900
I'll be on time for work tomorrow morning.

1262
00:52:34.100 --> 00:52:34.660
Don't you worry.

1263
00:52:35.340 --> 00:52:35.660
Wow.

1264
00:52:36.000 --> 00:52:36.420
I know.

1265
00:52:36.700 --> 00:52:39.900
Well, I was curious about what was in the shooting draft for this moment.

1266
00:52:39.900 --> 00:52:46.380
And this is what it says, an ambulance pulls out of the parking lot, lights flashing, sirens

1267
00:52:46.380 --> 00:52:46.940
