So I couldn't be there.

1284
00:53:30.360 --> 00:53:33.740
That's why one reason why I'm not there is because he was going to come type.

1285
00:53:34.120 --> 00:53:37.840
And, you know, I don't know if you saw this in the shooting draft, but the very end of

1286
00:53:37.840 --> 00:53:42.280
this episode, the camera was going to swing over to your computer screen.

1287
00:53:42.480 --> 00:53:44.700
And we were going to see what D'Angelo had typed.

1288
00:53:45.040 --> 00:53:45.300
Yes.

1289
00:53:45.380 --> 00:53:48.960
And even though he was speaking gibberish, he would have typed, Jenna, you have it, right?

1290
00:53:49.080 --> 00:53:49.580
I have it.

1291
00:53:49.660 --> 00:53:51.420
This is what would have been the last shot.

1292
00:53:52.400 --> 00:53:53.200
Please help.

1293
00:53:53.440 --> 00:53:56.220
I am of sound mind and I am a prisoner in my body.

1294
00:53:56.420 --> 00:54:01.200
My family is arranging to have power of attorney over me and intends to issue a DNR order.

1295
00:54:01.440 --> 00:54:02.940
This is not in my intereSt.

1296
00:54:03.240 --> 00:54:05.400
Please contact my lawyer, Fred Nestor.

1297
00:54:05.600 --> 00:54:09.120
His number is in my BlackBerry, which is on my dresser to the left of my watch.

1298
00:54:09.820 --> 00:54:10.260
Yeah.

1299
00:54:10.580 --> 00:54:10.840
Yeah.

1300
00:54:11.100 --> 00:54:12.340
That's how it would have ended.

1301
00:54:13.060 --> 00:54:15.760
Instead, it ends with them sort of escorting him out.

1302
00:54:16.380 --> 00:54:19.200
You guys, I couldn't keep it together in this scene.

1303
00:54:19.380 --> 00:54:20.780
You fully see me laugh.

1304
00:54:20.780 --> 00:54:28.500
You see me smile and laugh because, you know, they wrote out a few gibberish words for Will,

1305
00:54:28.620 --> 00:54:31.300
but then he mostly just started to make stuff up.

1306
00:54:31.500 --> 00:54:31.760
Yes.

1307
00:54:31.900 --> 00:54:35.780
And it was a little different each time and I couldn't keep it together.

1308
00:54:36.060 --> 00:54:38.880
I'm fully unprofessional at the end of this episode.

1309
00:54:39.220 --> 00:54:41.960
I'll put it in stories, but I totally break.

1310
00:54:42.220 --> 00:54:43.680
Well, I've got a time code for you.

1311
00:54:43.840 --> 00:54:44.680
Thanks to Nick N.

1312
00:54:44.800 --> 00:54:45.320
in Minnesota.

1313
00:54:45.680 --> 00:54:46.420
Did someone else see it?

1314
00:54:46.420 --> 00:54:48.740
Yeah, it's 21 minutes and 25 seconds.

1315
00:54:48.740 --> 00:54:55.640
And then almost right after that, Nick pointed out at 2135, right after Will makes a sneezing

1316
00:54:55.640 --> 00:54:59.920
noise, you can see John tilt his head down to the floor to try and hide his smile.

1317
00:55:00.120 --> 00:55:04.280
But his body language says that he broke into hysterical laughter the very moment the scene

1318
00:55:04.280 --> 00:55:04.700
cuts.

1319
00:55:07.060 --> 00:55:11.560
Well, before we say goodbye to this episode, Jenna, I wanted to read you an article I found

1320
00:55:11.560 --> 00:55:13.940
in the New York Times by Dave Itzkoff.

1321
00:55:14.360 --> 00:55:17.040
It came out April 6th of 2011.

1322
00:55:18.020 --> 00:55:23.040
He had come to set to interview Will Ferrell about being on The Office and about what this

1323
00:55:23.040 --> 00:55:25.060
meant for the show with Michael Scott leaving.

1324
00:55:25.540 --> 00:55:28.740
You and I have shared during this time there was a lot of uncertainty.

1325
00:55:29.460 --> 00:55:31.140
Well, here's what he said.

1326
00:55:31.650 --> 00:55:36.480
What the office producers may lack in clarity or candor about their vision for the show's

1327
00:55:36.480 --> 00:55:39.820
future, they amply make up for in nervousness.

1328
00:55:41.460 --> 00:55:48.300
Asked a few questions about a possible replacement for Mr. Correll, Mr. Lieberstein became agitated.

1329
00:55:49.200 --> 00:55:56.320
He started, stopped, and retracted his responses multiple times before settling on the following

1330
00:55:56.320 --> 00:55:56.900
answer.

1331
00:55:57.240 --> 00:56:00.940
We have decided to go past Steve with the cast we have.

1332
00:56:01.360 --> 00:56:03.420
Because of the cast we have.

1333
00:56:04.400 --> 00:56:05.160
Mm-hmm.

1334
00:56:05.820 --> 00:56:11.320
Even so, The Office is front-loading its May 19th finale with guest stars like Ricky Gervais

1335
00:56:11.320 --> 00:56:17.260
and Will Arnett while ratcheting up anticipation for an announcement of Michael Scott's full-time

1336
00:56:17.260 --> 00:56:17.800
replacement.

1337
00:56:18.140 --> 00:56:22.620
Well, I'll tell you this, lady, in anticipation of finishing out this season and moving into

1338
00:56:22.620 --> 00:56:28.460
next season, I have been digging as much as I can to try to find information on the behind-the-scenes

1339
00:56:28.960 --> 00:56:29.360
scuttlebutt.

1340
00:56:29.440 --> 00:56:29.800
Uh-huh.

1341
00:56:29.920 --> 00:56:33.800
And I found out some kind of fun things, and I'm excited to share, but I'm going to wait

1342
00:56:33.800 --> 00:56:35.280
until we kick off season eight.

1343
00:56:35.480 --> 00:56:36.660
Oh, my gosh, Jenna.

1344
00:56:36.940 --> 00:56:39.900
I love it when you get a bee in your bonnet.

1345
00:56:40.260 --> 00:56:44.800
I'm like, I remember a lot of things, but then I think there's things I don't know, and

1346
00:56:44.800 --> 00:56:46.040
I want to know.

1347
00:56:46.240 --> 00:56:47.280
Oh, well, I can't wait.

1348
00:56:47.300 --> 00:56:49.180
I will be looking forward to that.

1349
00:56:49.180 --> 00:56:56.200
I will say this, I did get pulled into Paul's office for a one-on-one where he asked my opinion

1350
00:56:56.200 --> 00:56:58.360
of who I thought should be the next manager.

1351
00:56:58.640 --> 00:56:58.840
Really?

1352
00:56:59.260 --> 00:56:59.480
Mm-hmm.

1353
00:56:59.720 --> 00:57:01.340
Oh, you've got to give all that up.

1354
00:57:01.440 --> 00:57:01.920
I'll share.

1355
00:57:02.160 --> 00:57:02.440
Okay.

1356
00:57:02.520 --> 00:57:03.360
I'll share for season eight.

1357
00:57:03.600 --> 00:57:05.860
Well, that was Inner Circle, and guess what?

1358
